---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import '../styles/global.css';
---

<BaseLayout title="Why choose Rutvik? | viknik.tech" description="A candid note from Rutvik Gulhane on product engineering, responsibility, and building software around the people who use it.">
  <main>
    <section class="why-hero">
      <div class="why-hero__wash" aria-hidden="true"></div>
      <div class="container why-hero__grid">
        <div class="why-hero__copy">
          <span class="why-eyebrow">Why choose Rutvik?</span>
          <h1>I care.</h1>
          <p class="why-hero__lede">About the people using the software. About the company trusting me with its problems. About the thing I am building enough to stand behind it in production.</p>
          <p class="why-hero__aside">And yes, I care about being paid fairly for that responsibility.</p>
        </div>

        <!-- Replace this intentional space with an honest work photograph when one is ready. -->
        <div class="image-room" aria-label="Reserved space for a future Rutvik photograph">
          <span class="image-room__label">IMAGE ROOM</span>
          <div class="image-room__shape image-room__shape--one" aria-hidden="true"></div>
          <div class="image-room__shape image-room__shape--two" aria-hidden="true"></div>
          <p>A picture goes here.<br /><strong>Preferably one where I am actually doing the work.</strong></p>
          <small>Not urgently. The page can hold the thought until the right image exists.</small>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section translation-section">
      <div class="container container--narrow">
        <span class="why-eyebrow">What I actually do</span>
        <h2>Translate people problems into software.</h2>
        <p>That is not merely requirement gathering, a PRD, or a survey. If you treat it like a survey, people give you survey answers. The useful answers arrive when you are curious about their routine: what slows them down, what they still do manually on weekends, what frustrates them, and what they have quietly accepted as “just how work is.”</p>
        <p>A product engineer is the bridge between that reality and the software: user flow, interface, backend, deployment, and the awkward real-world parts in between.</p>
        <div class="translation-map" aria-label="How Rutvik approaches product engineering">
          <div><span>Listen properly</span><strong>Daily routine, workarounds, frustration.</strong></div>
          <b aria-hidden="true">→</b>
          <div><span>Choose the real problem</span><strong>What should change now—and what can wait.</strong></div>
          <b aria-hidden="true">→</b>
          <div><span>Carry the complexity</span><strong>Make the experience feel natural to use.</strong></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section section--alt philosophy-section">
      <div class="container container--narrow">
        <span class="why-eyebrow">My philosophy</span>
        <h2>Software is people.</h2>
        <p>I first heard that idea from Coda Hale and took it to heart. The complexity underneath can be enormous. Infrastructure can be enormous. But users should not have to carry that cognitive burden.</p>
        <p>They should be able to use software through intuition, without their attention being overloaded. Attention is valuable. I try to protect it: fewer clicks, less visual clutter, and no manual required just to complete the task the software claims to solve.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section proof-section">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="proof-section__heading">
          <div>
            <span class="why-eyebrow">Proof, not a slogan</span>
            <h2>SpotBook</h2>
          </div>
          <a href="/projects/spotbook" class="btn btn--outline">See the case study →</a>
        </div>
        <div class="proof-grid">
          <article class="proof-card proof-card--wide">
            <span>THE PRODUCT DECISION</span>
            <h3>My competition was paper.</h3>
            <p>Paper was familiar, fast, and had been used in these businesses for generations. Replacing it meant the software had to feel easier than writing an order down—not merely more powerful.</p>
            <p>The mobile-first workflows took roughly ten minutes to teach sales agents and warehouse workers. Managers needed more time because they worked across the whole system; the people doing repeated work could understand their part quickly.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="proof-card proof-card--dark">
            <span>THE ENGINEERING UNDERNEATH</span>
            <h3>Safe enough for real money.</h3>
            <p>Spring Boot systems for concurrency-safe inventory, allocation, fulfillment, and production support—deployed on Railway so I could ship quickly and focus on the product.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="proof-card proof-card--coral">
            <span>THE MOMENT THAT CHANGED THE BAR</span>
            <h3>₹3.76 lakh vanished once.</h3>
            <p>One production mistake made the responsibility very real: other people’s money and trust were involved. The caution that followed later became confidence.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="proof-card proof-card--soft">
            <span>THE RESULT</span>
            <h3>₹9 crore in booked goods.</h3>
            <p>The app supported two expo seasons across multiple cities, handling roughly $1.1M of wholesale bookings.</p>
          </article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section work-section">
      <div class="container container--narrow">
        <span class="why-eyebrow">How I work</span>
        <h2>I carry the complexity underneath.</h2>
        <p>When I take responsibility for a people problem, I try to carry the complexity underneath it. The burden should sit with the system and with me—not with the person trying to do their work.</p>
        <p>I learn quickly, take ownership naturally, and work comfortably across product engineering, backend systems, and production support.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section section--alt fit-section">
      <div class="container container--narrow">
        <span class="why-eyebrow">Where I fit</span>
        <h2>Product engineer at heart.</h2>
        <p>I also fit full-stack engineering, backend engineering, and production/support roles where ownership matters.</p>
        <div class="fit-list" aria-label="Roles Rutvik fits">
          <span>Product engineer</span><span>Full-stack engineer</span><span>Backend engineer</span><span>Production / support engineer</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section closing-section">
      <div class="container container--narrow">
        <span class="why-eyebrow">The practical bits</span>
        <h2>The work above shows how I think. My resume shows what I have done.</h2>
        <div class="closing-section__actions">
          <a href="/Rutvik_Gulhane_Product_Engineer_Resume.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="btn btn--primary">Download Product Engineering Resume ↓</a>
          <a href="/contact" class="btn btn--outline">Let’s talk →</a>
        </div>
        <p class="closing-section__note">If you are building something for people and need someone you can trust with an important part of it, let’s talk.</p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .why-hero { position: relative; overflow: hidden; padding: calc(76px + var(--space-3xl)) 0 var(--space-3xl); background: var(--bg-cream); }
  .why-hero__wash { position: absolute; inset: 0; background: radial-gradient(circle at 80% 28%, color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent-pink) 23%, transparent), transparent 29%), radial-gradient(circle at 15% 82%, color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent-sky) 20%, transparent), transparent 35%); }
  .why-hero__grid { position: relative; display: grid; gap: var(--space-2xl); align-items: center; }
  .why-hero__copy { max-width: 700px; }
  .why-eyebrow { display: block; margin-bottom: var(--space-md); color: var(--accent-violet); font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: var(--text-xs); font-weight: 800; letter-spacing: 0.09em; text-transform: uppercase; }
  .why-hero h1 { margin-bottom: var(--space-md); font-size: clamp(5rem, 14vw, 11.5rem); line-height: 0.8; letter-spacing: -0.09em; }
  .why-hero__lede { margin: 0; font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: clamp(var(--text-xl), 3vw, var(--text-3xl)); font-weight: 700; line-height: 1.15; }
  .why-hero__aside { margin: var(--space-lg) 0 0; color: var(--text-muted); font-size: var(--text-base); }
  .image-room { position: relative; display: grid; min-height: 380px; align-content: end; padding: var(--space-xl); overflow: hidden; border: 1px dashed color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent-violet) 55%, var(--bg-cream-darker)); border-radius: var(--radius-xl); background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--bg-cream) 80%, white); box-shadow: var(--shadow-sm); }
  .image-room__label { position: absolute; top: var(--space-md); left: var(--space-md); color: var(--accent-violet); font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: var(--text-xs); font-weight: 800; letter-spacing: 0.1em; }
  .image-room p { position: relative; max-width: 260px; margin: 0; font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: var(--text-xl); line-height: 1.1; }
  .image-room small { position: relative; max-width: 260px; margin-top: var(--space-md); color: var(--text-muted); font-size: var(--text-xs); line-height: 1.55; }
  .image-room__shape { position: absolute; width: 190px; height: 190px; border-radius: 43% 57% 55% 45% / 40% 39% 61% 60%; opacity: 0.55; }
  .image-room__shape--one { top: 18%; right: 12%; background: var(--accent-sky); transform: rotate(21deg); }
  .image-room__shape--two { top: 31%; right: 29%; width: 125px; height: 125px; background: var(--accent-amber); transform: rotate(-13deg); }
  .translation-section h2, .philosophy-section h2, .work-section h2, .fit-section h2, .closing-section h2 { max-width: 810px; margin-bottom: var(--space-lg); font-size: clamp(var(--text-3xl), 5vw, var(--text-5xl)); line-height: 0.98; }
  .translation-section p, .philosophy-section p, .work-section p, .fit-section p { max-width: 760px; font-size: var(--text-lg); line-height: 1.8; }
  .translation-section p + p, .philosophy-section p + p, .work-section p + p { margin-top: var(--space-lg); }
  .translation-map { display: grid; gap: var(--space-sm); margin-top: var(--space-2xl); padding: var(--space-md); border: 1px solid var(--bg-cream-darker); border-radius: var(--radius-lg); background: var(--bg-cream-dark); }
  .translation-map div { display: grid; gap: var(--space-xs); padding: var(--space-md); border-radius: var(--radius-md); background: var(--bg-cream); }
  .translation-map span, .proof-card > span { color: var(--accent-violet); font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: var(--text-xs); font-weight: 800; letter-spacing: 0.06em; text-transform: uppercase; }
  .translation-map strong { font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: var(--text-base); line-height: 1.35; }
  .translation-map > b { align-self: center; justify-self: center; color: var(--accent-violet); }
  .proof-section { border-top: 1px solid var(--bg-cream-darker); }
  .proof-section__heading { display: flex; align-items: end; justify-content: space-between; gap: var(--space-lg); margin-bottom: var(--space-xl); }
  .proof-section__heading h2 { margin: 0; font-size: clamp(var(--text-4xl), 7vw, var(--text-6xl)); line-height: 0.9; }
  .proof-grid { display: grid; gap: var(--space-md); }
  .proof-card { min-height: 230px; padding: var(--space-xl); border: 1px solid var(--bg-cream-darker); border-radius: var(--radius-xl); background: var(--bg-cream-dark); }
  .proof-card h3 { margin: var(--space-md) 0; font-size: var(--text-2xl); line-height: 1.02; }
  .proof-card p { margin: 0; color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.7; }
  .proof-card p + p { margin-top: var(--space-md); }
  .proof-card--dark { background: var(--text-primary); border-color: var(--text-primary); color: var(--bg-cream); }
  .proof-card--dark > span { color: var(--accent-amber); }
  .proof-card--dark p { color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--bg-cream) 80%, transparent); }
  .proof-card--coral { background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent-coral) 80%, var(--bg-cream)); }
  .proof-card--coral > span { color: var(--text-primary); }
  .proof-card--soft { background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent-sky) 20%, var(--bg-cream)); }
  .fit-list { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: var(--space-sm); margin-top: var(--space-xl); }
  .fit-list span { padding: 0.65rem 0.85rem; border: 1px solid var(--bg-cream-darker); border-radius: var(--radius-full); background: var(--bg-cream); font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: var(--text-xs); font-weight: 700; }
  .closing-section { text-align: center; }
  .closing-section h2 { margin-inline: auto; }
  .closing-section__actions { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; justify-content: center; gap: var(--space-md); margin-top: var(--space-xl); }
  .closing-section__note { max-width: 620px; margin: var(--space-2xl) auto 0; color: var(--text-muted); font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: var(--text-xl); line-height: 1.3; }
  @media (min-width: 768px) { .why-hero__grid { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.45fr) minmax(280px, 0.8fr); } .translation-map { grid-template-columns: 1fr auto 1fr auto 1fr; align-items: stretch; } .proof-grid { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); } .proof-card--wide { grid-column: span 2; } }
  @media (max-width: 640px) { .why-hero { padding-top: calc(65px + var(--space-2xl)); } .image-room { min-height: 300px; } .proof-section__heading { align-items: start; flex-direction: column; } .proof-card { min-height: auto; padding: var(--space-lg); } .closing-section__actions { flex-direction: column; align-items: stretch; } }
</style>
